  "summary": "The released 1.1.0 portable evidence kit includes metadata-bound revalidation queues: prioritize blocked critical tests, see exact freshness deadlines, identify missing procedures and preserve the source and baseline revisions needed for review.",
  "rationale": "The original requirement/test/fault traceability, SQL cross-check, export formats and immutable local history are retained. The extracted app verifies a failed critical test, an independently calculated first-invalid timestamp, missing-procedure guidance and an exact JSON download. It turns declared evidence gaps into a practical human review queue without waiving gates or pretending to execute tests.",
  "limitations": [
    "Declared synthetic evidence consistency only; SQL agreement does not authenticate provenance or reveal omitted requirements.",
    "The queue plans human review; it does not execute tests, waive release gates or establish flight qualification.",
    "Unsigned desktop portable folders, not system installers or clean-machine proof. Three-OS extracted-native checks drive an owned URL; default OS browser opening remains manual."
  ],
